  "findings": [
    "Guest-heap arenas dominate swap in BOTH arms: 358.0 MiB (candidate) / 366.8 MiB (control) inside the largest anon VMA, ~70% of all swapped pages.",
    "A deterministic fully-cold 72.0 MiB anonymous mapping (0 MiB resident, 64.1 MiB swapped) appears in every collected run at a randomized host address.",
    "Second guest arena holds 41.3 / 59.4 MiB swapped; all remaining VMAs are <11 MiB each.",
    "The 720 arm keeps slightly lower total SwapPss at game-idle (509.1 vs 536.4 MiB) in this pair; sample size is two runs and phases are not identical."
  ],
  "next_steps": [
    "Identify the owner of the 72 MiB cold mapping (maps-diff across startup/menu/game-idle snapshots or a bounded host-mmap logger); releasing a proven-cold 64 MiB would remove ~12% of swap.",
    "Attribute the ~350-360 MiB of guest-heap swap with a lowered allocation-trace threshold (256 KiB) since >=4 MiB blocks are already proven sparse."
  ],
  "not_proven": [
    "reclaim safety of the 72 MiB mapping",
    "steady-state attribution of sub-4 MiB allocations",
    "any swapoff or discard"
  ]
